th pass, 5 if other submits; submit gives 0/4. With correlation p (P(other pass | I pass)) = p, q = P(other pass | I submit). With high correlation, e.g. p≈q high... need 6p−10q>1 analog: payoff pass = 2p+5(1−p)=5−3p; submit = 0q+4(1−q)=4−4q. Pass better iff 5−3p > 4−4q iff 1 > 3p−4q. With strong correlation p≈q≈1, 3p−4q≈−1 <1 → pass better. With near-perfect correlation p=q: 1 > −p, always true. So pass.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5516,"completion_tokens":403,"total_tokens":5919,"cost":0.0010289,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0010289,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0008274,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0002015},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":224,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}